From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ThaRae <tharae@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:38:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] LibWeb: Only authorize a WebAuthn AppID on the caller's own
 host

The FIDO algorithm for determining if a caller's FacetID is
authorized for an AppID authorizes the caller only when the AppID's
trusted facet list names the caller's facet. The shortcut here let a
caller pass without any list at all when its host merely shares the
AppID host's registrable domain, so https://evil.example.com could
run an assertion ceremony with the AppID of
https://login.example.com: it could probe whether the user holds the
U2F credential that RP associated with login.example.com's AppID,
and collect signatures over challenges of its choosing (the
assertion still names the attacker's origin in clientDataJSON, so it
doesn't impersonate the victim host). On user-content subdomains,
one origin under a site can do this against every other.

Until the trusted facet list is fetched and checked, the same-origin
shortcut other browsers use is the only safe one: the caller's host
must equal the AppID's host.
---
 Libraries/LibWeb/WebAuthn/PublicKeyCredential.cpp | 9 +--------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Libraries/LibWeb/WebAuthn/PublicKeyCredential.cpp b/Libraries/LibWeb/WebAuthn/PublicKeyCredential.cpp
index 09cbe7c8d8cce45499ba13d989f1bb361a7a8a35..6b5c49f2bb0d90c496e3210b776691917f1a19e5 100644
--- a/Libraries/LibWeb/WebAuthn/PublicKeyCredential.cpp
+++ b/Libraries/LibWeb/WebAuthn/PublicKeyCredential.cpp
@@ -622,14 +622,7 @@ static bool is_a_caller_s_facet_id_authorized_for_an_app_id(URL::Origin const& c
     if (caller_origin.is_opaque() || caller_origin.scheme().value_or({}) != "https"sv)
         return false;
 
-    auto const& caller_host = caller_origin.host();
-    auto const& app_id_host = *app_id_url->host();
-    if (caller_host == app_id_host)
-        return true;
-
-    auto caller_registrable_domain = caller_host.registrable_domain();
-    auto app_id_registrable_domain = app_id_host.registrable_domain();
-    return caller_registrable_domain.has_value() && caller_registrable_domain == app_id_registrable_domain;
+    return caller_origin.host() == *app_id_url->host();
 }
 
 // https://w3c.github.io/webauthn/#sctn-discover-from-external-source
